Implement the ticket below. Treat the primary ticket as the task to complete, and use the parent ticket for background, scope and constraints.

When the implementation is done:

1. Run the project's own checks (lint, types, tests) for what you changed and fix what fails.
2. Commit your work. Start every commit message with the ticket key.
3. Push the branch and open a draft pull request with `gh pr create --draft`. Use `<ticket key> <ticket summary>` as the title. Keep the description to a few short bullet points saying what changed; no testing or reproduction steps.
4. Stop there and tell me the pull request is ready for my review. Do not mark it ready for review, merge it, or change the ticket in Jira.

If a pull request for this branch already exists, push to it instead of opening a new one.

